{
  "comment": [
    "Every supported native ABI symbol has exactly one Python owner and at",
    "least one production caller. A symbol without a caller is cleanup debt,",
    "not a feature: it creates no coverage or release requirement.",
    "",
    "library and logical_owner are now the SAME string, _radar_native. Phase 4",
    "recorded a different physical artifact stem next to the logical owner name",
    "and deferred the rename to Phase 10, which executed it (R-ADR-004). Both",
    "keys are kept because a single value cannot say whether a future artifact",
    "stem has drifted away from the owner it is supposed to be.",
    "",
    "Schema 2 (Phase 10, work items 3-4) turns this from a coverage manifest",
    "into an OWNERSHIP REGISTRY. Seven per-operator columns were added:",
    "",
    "  native_tu         the translation unit that owns the numerics. The",
    "                    registration itself lives in extension.cpp for every",
    "                    symbol, so naming that file would carry no ownership",
    "                    information at all.",
    "  numerical_owner   who owns the arithmetic. Must be 'radar' in THIS",
    "                    manifest: item 4 forbids registering a RayD-owned or",
    "                    Channel-owned family as a Radar shared primitive, and",
    "                    a column makes that a checkable value rather than an",
    "                    unwritten rule. RayD and Channel numerics reach Radar",
    "                    as compact typed CUDA tensors through the consumer",
    "                    contract, never as linked code (R-ADR-004).",
    "  ad_role           primal / backward / jvp / utility.",
    "  ad_group          the AD family the role belongs to. Exactly one primal",
    "                    per group, so a companion registered without its",
    "                    primal - or a primal quietly replaced - is visible.",
    "  launches          CUDA kernel launches per operator call, counted in the",
    "                    kernel source. R-ADR-004 pins the two_way_join family",
    "                    at one launch each way; the rest are transcribed from",
    "                    the launch sites in native_tu.",
    "  fused_stages      the device stages fused into those launches, named",
    "                    after the kernel's own device helpers. This is what",
    "                    makes 'do not split a fused operation' reviewable.",
    "  host_observations host reads (.item/.cpu/.tolist/.numpy) the operator",
    "                    performs. Zero for all 28, which is R-ADR-006's 'Radar",
    "                    adds zero host observations' made machine-readable.",
    "                    The sanctioned freeze-time reads live in",
    "                    witwin/radar/paths.py, which is not a native",
    "                    operator and has no row here.",
    "",
    "frontend_quantize is a one-member ad_group on purpose: the ADC sits below",
    "R-ADR-018's non-differentiability wall and refuses a differentiable input,",
    "so it ships no backward and no jvp. That is a declared state, not a gap.",
    "",
    "error_owners is Radar's answer to Channel's single CapacityFailureState",
    "owner: one row per failure domain, naming the module that raises and what",
    "it guarantees about partial results."
  ],
  "schema_version": 2,
  "radar_abi_version": 3,
